    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is delighted to present No. 57B Sidmonton Gardens to the market. This charming first-floor, own-door apartment offers a particularly appealing combination of well-presented accommodation together with designated outdoor space to both the front and rear.\n\nThe garden areas associated with No. 57B provide a wonderful addition to the apartment and offer purchasers the opportunity to enjoy their own outdoor space, a feature not always readily available with apartment living. \n\nThis may particularly appeal to buyers who enjoy gardening, those looking to downsize without giving up outdoor space, or anyone seeking the convenience of apartment living with the added benefit of a garden area.\n\nThe well-presented and light-filled accommodation extends to approximately 58 sq. m. located on the top floor ans accessed via a seperate doorway at the side of the proprty. It comprises of an entrance hall with tiled flooring and steps leading down to the hall door. The living room overlooks the front and is open-plan to the kitchen, which enjoys an outlook towards the rear.\nThe living room offers ample space for both comfortable seating and a dining area. The kitchen is fitted with a good selection of cabinets together with generous countertop space for food preparation.\n\nOff the hallway is a shower room and two double bedrooms. Bedroom 1 benefits from an en-suite shower room, while Bedroom 2 features a walk-in closet. This space was originally accessed from Bedroom 1 and could potentially be reinstated to that configuration if desired.\nA spacious attic, accessed via a pull-down ladder, is floored and provides useful storage space.\n\nOutside, No. 57B benefits from designated garden areas to both the front and rear, together with a designated parking space. The front garden area is laid in lawn with mature planting, while the rear garden area provides further private outdoor space associated with No. 57B. There is also a block-built shed providing useful additional storage.\n\nThe location is superb. Bray Seafront is approximately 500m away, while Bray DART station and bus terminus are approximately 1km from the property. With the town's excellent selection of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants, public transport and recreational amenities all within easy reach, No. 57B offers a highly convenient location close to both Bray town centre and the seafront.\n\nPersonal inspection is highly recommended to appreciate the well-presented accommodation, convenient location and valuable outdoor space offered by this attractive property.\n\nKey Features\n\n• Two-bedroom first-floor apartment with attic storage space\n• Accommodation extending to approximately 58 sq. m.\n• Own-door access\n• Designated off-street parking space\n• Designated garden areas to the front and rear associated with No. 57B\n• Block-built storage shed\n• Gas-fired central heating\n• Double-glazed windows\n• Solid-fuel stove in living room\n• Two double bedrooms\n• Two shower rooms\n• Excellent location close to Bray town centre\n• Approximately 1km walk to Bray DART station and bus terminus\n• Approximately 500m from Bray Seafront"
      },
      {
